From 591d4a026a024e5a93aa4a06fdba578ea876eee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:10:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Skip triage-park evidence only on genuinely unsynced
 boards

Review of e2a2ea reproduced (deleg_ed307335): on a synced board a peer can
promote/claim/park, or directly park, a home-created triage card on probe P
while this home still sees triage; the home's direct triage -> scheduled park
then skipped the reset and, after delivery, the peer's same-P re-park yielded
(t0, 2) instead of (t0+3600, 1).

The no-evidence skip now requires durable local sync state to be absent
(kanban_db_sync.sync_state, read inside the park's transaction; never config).
On a synced board the direct triage park carries the reset barrier and snapshot
inline in its own scheduled payload, so test_kanban_triage_park's six atomic
cardinality cases (which run on a SYNCED board, not unsynced) still append one
event. The transaction that creates kanban_sync_state (moved into the existing
install_or_remove write_txn) clears every freshness marker; later enabled inits
do not.

Proof: test_kanban_wake_episode_triage_sync.py on e2a2ea prod code: 4 FAILED,
1 passed (unsynced control); GREEN 5/5 here. Both real-API delayed foreign
triage routes, created-unsynced then enable-sync, synced-at-create. Mutations
9/9 killed (mut-triage-sync.log). Broad previous 65 files + new: 66 files,
863 passed, 0 failed, retries 0.

Boundary: an unsynced board copied to another host by a non-sync path (file
copy/restore) can still have a foreign episode the skipped park never clears;
a board whose sync row exists in any mode (including detached 'off') is
treated as synced.
